NNAAMMEE
       e2label - Change the label on an ext2/ext3/ext4 file system

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ee22llaabbeell _d_e_v_i_c_e [ _v_o_l_u_m_e_-_l_a_b_e_l ]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ee22llaabbeell  will  display or change the volume label on the ext2, ext3, or
       ext4 file system located on _d_e_v_i_c_e_.

       If the optional argument _v_o_l_u_m_e_-_l_a_b_e_l is not present, ee22llaabbeell will sim‐
       ply display the current volume label.

       If the optional argument _v_o_l_u_m_e_-_l_a_b_e_l is present, then ee22llaabbeell will set
       the volume label to be _v_o_l_u_m_e_-_l_a_b_e_l.  Ext2 volume labels can be at most
       16 characters long; if _v_o_l_u_m_e_-_l_a_b_e_l is longer than 16 characters, ee22llaa‐‐
       bbeell will truncate it and print a warning message.  For other file  sys‐
       tems  that  support  online  label manipulation and are mounted ee22llaabbeell
       will work as well, but it will not attempt to truncate the _v_o_l_u_m_e_-_l_a_b_e_l
       at all.

       It  is  also  possible  to  set the volume label using the --LL option of
       ttuunnee22ffss(8).

